id: pm-review-bun-closeout-copy
title: Investigate intermittent native Bun closeout copy failure
description: Packed acceptance on Node 22 reached the native Bun closeout smoke test and returned workspace-copy/ENOENT. Envelope verdict assertions had already passed. The same code passed both packed checks on Node 26. Cause is not established; investigate disposable copy stability without weakening artifact-link policy.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-review#46"
created_at: "2026-10-23T17:48:22.873Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T00:40:54.314Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-review-epic
repro_steps: "Inspect https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/actions/runs/39996625199/job/120561709283 and compare the successful Node 26 packed executions at the same code commit 82f0c24. Run packed npm/Bun acceptance repeatedly in isolated consumers to determine which copy entry disappears."
expected_result: Native Bun closeout prepares a stable disposable workspace or a precise actionable refusal.
actual_result: "CI run 39996625199, attempt 1: test (22) packed acceptance failed at closeout preparation with execution_missing and workspace-copy/ENOENT; test (26), including Bun release gates, passed."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T00:26:35.596Z",codex-agent,"Reusing this existing intermittent copy issue for the orchestrator-reported Node 22 packed closeout failure in CI run 40342564725, job 121640877263. Focused packed Node 22 reproduction is running; investigating the exact missing copy entry before changing policy or acceptance assertions."
  "2026-10-27T00:39:13.848Z",codex-agent,"The initial Node 22 packed suite and 30 ordinary focused retries passed, confirming the intermittent nature. A deterministic packed-consumer schedule now reproduces workspace-copy/ENOENT by retiring the owned fixture .pm-cli/runtime/telemetry/closeout-fixture-retiring.tmp after copy enumeration and before reading it. HOME equals the consumer workspace, so SDK global telemetry is accidentally treated as project source. Fix excludes the SDK-resolved global tracker before traversal; unrelated .pm-cli project source remains included. Other disappearing workspace entries receive a bounded relative ENTRY_DISAPPEARED diagnostic and retry remedy. No telemetry settings change."
  "2026-10-27T00:40:54.314Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: removed only the SDK global-root exclusion from executeCloseout and ran node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='SDK global tracker discovery' test/closeout-round.test.ts. It failed exit 1 with workspace-copy/ARTIFACT_SYMLINK for the live global runtime fixture; restored source passes. Node 22 focused packed command node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern='packed closeout excludes' --test-reporter=spec test/install.acceptance.ts now passes 1/1; the same injected retirement on the old packed code failed with the review's workspace-copy/ENOENT. Targeted diagnostic and round suites passed 12/12. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gate pass at unchanged thresholds."
